2
00:05:23,845 --> 00:05:36,015
出会えた奇跡にもう息がとまりそうだよ
It feels like my breath stops at the miracle of meeting you...

3
00:05:45,642 --> 00:05:58,262
何を見ているの？ どこまでも澄んだ瞳で
What are you looking at with eyes so clear...

4
00:05:58,262 --> 00:06:13,862
二人だけが触われる世界で きっとすべてがいま始まるから
In a world that only the two of us can touch, surely everything is beginning right now.

5
00:06:17,422 --> 00:06:29,682
君に会うために生まれたと伝えたいんだ
I want to tell you I was born just to meet you.

6
00:06:30,262 --> 00:06:47,992
粗野な風も 胸刺す視線も 全部 ひりひりする声になるのさ ずっと
Even the rough wind, even the piercing gazes, all turn into a stinging voice, forever...

7
00:06:53,762 --> 00:07:15,002
キミヲアイシテル 濁りのない好きって気持ちは 振り返るものなんてない 二人きり未来さえ飛べるんだ
I love you. A feeling of unclouded love looks back at nothing; the two of us can leap even beyond the future.

8
00:07:22,672 --> 00:07:35,012
どこへゆくの？ 小さな自分に 涙あふれるけど走りだせる
Where are you going? Tears overflow within my small self, but I can start running.

9
00:07:53,092 --> 00:08:05,762
もしもはぐれたら身体ごと散ってみせる
If we get separated, I'll scatter my whole body to prove it.

10
00:08:06,792 --> 00:08:23,062
花びらたった一枚の姿になって 君の愛求めて旅するよ ずっと
Becoming the form of a single flower petal, I will journey searching for your love, forever.

11
00:08:25,082 --> 00:08:55,942
キミヲダキシメル 汚されない好きって気持ちが 時を超えて呼び合う 二人きり未来へと飛べたんだ
I hold you close. An unblemished feeling of love calls out across time; the two of us could fly toward the future.

12
00:08:57,872 --> 00:09:10,132
出会えた奇跡にもう息がとまりそうだよ
It feels like my breath stops at the miracle of meeting you...

13
00:09:11,202 --> 00:09:24,692
つないだその手に少し強くなれる気がする
Holding your connected hand, I feel like I can grow a little stronger.

14
00:09:25,452 --> 00:09:48,252
出会えた奇跡にもう息がとまりそうだよ 明日も未来も…ただ、どうしようもなく、好きだよ
It feels like my breath stops at the miracle of meeting you... Tomorrow and the future too... I just love you beyond help.

15
00:10:20,526 --> 00:10:29,066
いつか僕らの上をスレスレに通りすぎていったあの飛行機を
That airplane that passed by us so closely overhead one day...

16
00:10:29,256 --> 00:10:39,076
不思議なくらいに憶えてる 意味もないのに 何故か
I remember it so strangely, for no reason at all.

17
00:10:39,726 --> 00:10:48,816
不甲斐なくて泣いた日の夜に ただ強くなりたいと願ってた
On the night when I cried in my helplessness, I just wished to become strong.

18
00:10:49,026 --> 00:10:54,266
そのために必要な勇気を探し求めていた
I was searching and seeking the courage needed for that.

19
00:10:54,266 --> 00:10:58,606
残酷な運命が定まっているとして
Even if a cruel destiny is set,

20
00:10:58,976 --> 00:11:03,566
それがいつの日か僕の前に現れるとして
And even if it appears before me one day,

21
00:11:03,646 --> 00:11:08,786
ただ一瞬 この一瞬 息ができるなら
If I could just breathe for a single moment, this very moment,

22
00:11:09,036 --> 00:11:13,506
どうでもいいと思えた その心を
I felt that nothing else mattered, that heart of mine...

23
00:11:13,506 --> 00:11:20,176
もう一度 遠くへ行け 遠くへ行けと 僕の中で誰かが歌う
Someone inside me sings: Go further away once more, go further away.

24
00:11:20,446 --> 00:11:25,006
どうしようもないほど熱烈に いつだって目を腫らした君が二度と悲しまないように笑える
So overwhelmingly passionate, so that you, with eyes swollen from crying, can smile and never be sad again...

25
00:11:25,006 --> 00:11:29,156
さらば掲げろ ピースサイン 転がっていくストーリーを
Farewell, hold up your peace sign, as the story rolls on.

26
00:11:34,856 --> 00:11:39,816
「守りたい」だなんて言えるほど 君が弱くはないの分かってた
I knew you weren't so weak that you could say 'I want to protect you'.

27
00:11:39,906 --> 00:11:44,476
それ以上に僕は弱くてさ 君が大事だったんだ
More than that, I was weak, and you were precious to me.

28
00:11:44,476 --> 00:11:49,396
「一人で生きていくんだ」なんてさ 口を突いて叫んだあの日から
Ever since that day when I blurted out and shouted that I would live all alone,

29
00:11:49,396 --> 00:11:54,066
変わっていく僕を笑えばいい 独りが怖い僕を
You can laugh at me changing, me who was so afraid of being alone.

30
00:11:54,196 --> 00:12:03,036
蹴飛ばして 噛み付いて 息もできなくて 騒ぐ頭と 腹の奥が くしゃくしゃになったって
Kicking and biting back, unable to even breathe, my churning head and stomach becoming a complete mess...

31
00:12:03,196 --> 00:12:07,806
衒いも外連も消えてしまうくらいに
To the point where all pretense and flashiness disappear,

32
00:12:07,806 --> 00:12:13,836
今は触っていたいんだ 君の心に
Right now I want to touch your heart.

33
00:12:14,406 --> 00:12:24,236
僕たちはきっといつか 遠く離れた太陽にすら手が届いて 夜明け前を手に入れて笑おう
We will surely reach far away one day, even touching the distant sun, and grab hold of the dawn to laugh.

34
00:12:24,236 --> 00:12:34,076
そうやって青く燃える色に染まり 朧げな街の向こうへ 手を繋いで走って行けるはずだ
Dyeing ourselves in the color of burning blue, heading beyond the hazy town, we should be able to run hand in hand.

35
00:12:34,266 --> 00:12:39,936
君と未来を盗み描く 捻りのないストーリーを
Stealing and drawing the future with you, a straightforward story without any twists.

36
00:12:49,636 --> 00:12:54,706
瘡蓋だらけ 荒くれた日々が 削り削られ 擦切れた今が
The days full of scabs and roughness, the now worn out and scraped away...

37
00:12:54,806 --> 00:12:58,906
君の言葉で蘇る 鮮やかにも 現れてく
Revived by your words, vividly appearing once again.

38
00:12:59,096 --> 00:13:06,756
蛹のままで 眠る魂も 食べかけのまま 捨てたあの夢を もう一度 取り戻せ
The soul sleeping as a chrysalis, the dream cast aside half-eaten—take them back once more.

39
00:13:25,655 --> 00:13:28,155
もう一度
Once more...

40
00:13:28,155 --> 00:13:32,155
遠くへ行け 遠くへ行けと 僕の中で誰かが歌う
Go further away, go further away, someone inside me sings.

41
00:13:32,155 --> 00:13:36,655
どうしようもないほど熱烈に
So overwhelmingly passionate...

42
00:13:36,655 --> 00:13:41,655
いつだって目を腫らした君が二度と悲しまないように笑える そんなヒーローになるための歌
So that you, with eyes swollen from crying, can smile and never be sad again—a song to become that kind of hero.

43
00:13:41,655 --> 00:13:51,655
さらば掲げろ ピースサイン 転がっていくストーリーを
Farewell, hold up your peace sign, as the story rolls on.

44
00:13:51,655 --> 00:13:59,655
君と未来を盗み描く 捻りのないストーリーを
Stealing and drawing the future with you, a straightforward story without any twists.

45
00:14:08,476 --> 00:14:12,166
考えたって分からないし 青空の下、君を待った
Thinking it over gets me nowhere, so I waited for you under the blue sky.

46
00:14:12,166 --> 00:14:16,666
風が吹いた正午、昼下がりを抜け出す想像
At noon when the wind blew, imagining slipping away from the lazy afternoon...

47
00:14:16,666 --> 00:14:20,566
ねぇ、これからどうなるんだろうね 進め方教わらないんだよ
Hey, I wonder what will happen from here on out? Nobody ever taught us how to move forward.

48
00:14:20,566 --> 00:14:24,066
君の目を見た 何も言えず僕は歩いた
I looked into your eyes and walked away without saying a word.

49
00:14:24,066 --> 00:14:27,155
[Title: だから僕は音楽を辞めた]
[Title: Then I Hated Music]

50
00:14:39,206 --> 00:14:43,076
考えたって分からないし 青春なんてつまらないし
Thinking it over gets me nowhere, and youth is so boring.

51
00:14:43,076 --> 00:14:46,476
辞めた筈のピアノ、机を弾く癖が抜けない
The piano I should have quit—I still catch myself tapping on the desk.

52
00:14:46,476 --> 00:14:50,166
ねぇ、将来何してるだろうね 音楽はしてないといいね
Hey, I wonder what I'll be doing in the future? I hope I'm not making music anymore.

53
00:14:50,166 --> 00:14:52,976
困らないでよ
Please don't trouble me.

54
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,708
心の中に一つ線を引いても どうしても消えなかった
Even if I draw a single line in my heart, it just wouldn't fade away.

55
00:15:03,608 --> 00:15:06,608
今更なんだから なぁ、もう思い出すな
It's too late now, hey, stop remembering already.

56
00:15:08,108 --> 00:15:13,108
間違ってるんだよ わかってないよ、あんたら人間も
You're wrong. You don't get it, you humans either.

57
00:15:13,608 --> 00:15:17,408
本当も愛も世界も苦しさも人生も
Truth, love, the world, suffering, and life—

58
00:15:17,408 --> 00:15:21,108
どうでもいいよ 正しいかどうか知りたいのだって防衛本能だ
none of that matters. Wanting to know whether something is right is just self-defense.

59
00:15:21,108 --> 00:15:24,108
考えたんだ あんたのせいだ
I thought about it, and it's all your fault.

60
00:15:38,808 --> 00:15:43,608
考えたってわからないが、本当に年老いたくないんだ
Thinking won't give me answers, but I really don't want to grow old.

61
00:15:43,608 --> 00:15:46,608
いつか死んだらって思うだけで胸が空っぽになるんだ
Just thinking about dying someday makes my chest feel completely empty.

62
00:15:46,608 --> 00:15:50,608
将来何してるだろうって 大人になったらわかったよ
Wondering what I'd be doing in the future—I finally understood once I became an adult.

63
00:15:52,108 --> 00:15:59,608
何もしてないさ 幸せな顔した人が憎いのは
I'm doing nothing at all. What I resent are people with happy faces—

64
00:16:00,608 --> 00:16:06,108
どう割り切ったらいいんだ 満たされない頭の奥の
How am I supposed to accept this, deep inside my unsatisfied mind

65
00:16:06,608 --> 00:16:11,108
化け物みたいな劣等感
an inferiority complex like a monster.

66
00:16:11,408 --> 00:16:14,608
間違ってないよ なぁ、何だかんだあんたら人間だ
I'm not wrong. After all, you humans are human too.

67
00:16:14,608 --> 00:16:18,608
愛も救いも優しさも根拠がないなんて
Saying love, salvation, and kindness have no basis—

68
00:16:18,608 --> 00:16:24,108
ラブソングなんかが痛いのだって防衛本能だ どうでもいいか あんたのせいだ
Love songs hurting is just self-defense. Whatever, it's your fault.

69
00:16:40,608 --> 00:16:43,608
考えたってわからないし 生きてるだけでも苦しいし
Thinking won't give me answers, just living is painful,

70
00:16:43,608 --> 00:16:47,608
音楽とか儲からないし 歌詞とか適当でもいいよ
music doesn't make money, and lyrics or whatever can be casual.

71
00:16:50,608 --> 00:16:54,608
どうでもいいんだ 間違ってないだろ
It doesn't matter. I'm not wrong, am I?

72
00:16:54,608 --> 00:17:04,608
間違ってないよな 間違ってないよな 間違ってないよな
I'm not wrong, am I? I'm not wrong, am I? I'm not wrong, am I?

73
00:17:16,108 --> 00:17:20,108
間違ってるんだよ わかってるんだ あんたら人間も
You're wrong, I get it, you humans too.

74
00:17:20,608 --> 00:17:27,608
本当も愛も救いも優しさも人生もどうでもいいんだ 正しい答えが言えないのだって防衛本能だ どうでもいいや あんたのせいだ
Truth, love, salvation, kindness, and life—none of it matters. Not being able to give the right answer is just self-defense. Whatever, it's your fault.

75
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:51,108
僕だって信念があった 今じゃ塵みたいな想いだ
I used to have convictions too; now they feel like dust-like memories.

76
00:17:51,108 --> 00:17:55,608
何度でも君を書いた 売れることこそがどうでもよかったんだ
I drew you countless times. Selling out was the last thing that mattered.

77
00:17:56,608 --> 00:18:00,608
本当だ 本当なんだ 昔はそうだった
It's true, it's really true, it used to be like that.

78
00:18:02,108 --> 00:18:09,108
だから僕は音楽を辞めた
That's why I gave up on music.

79
00:18:18,608 --> 00:18:24,608
今なんじゃない? メラメラとたぎれ 眠っているだけの正義
Isn't it time? Blaze up, justice that's just lying dormant.

80
00:18:25,608 --> 00:18:31,608
こんな僕も君のヒーローになりたいのさ
Even someone like me wants to be your hero!

81
00:18:32,608 --> 00:18:36,608
Mela!

82
00:18:47,608 --> 00:18:53,608
かっこいい君には 僕じゃ頼りないのかなんて
For someone as cool as you, maybe I'm not reliable enough...

83
00:18:54,608 --> 00:19:00,608
そりゃそうだよな だって今もこうして迷ってる
Of course you'd think that, because I'm still hesitating like this.

84
00:19:03,108 --> 00:19:06,608
手を取ってくれないか
Won't you take my hand?

85
00:19:06,608 --> 00:19:10,108
ギブとテイクさ
It's give and take.

86
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:14,108
君が僕のヒーローだったように
Just like you were my hero,

87
00:19:14,608 --> 00:19:22,608
今なんじゃない? メラメラとたぎる こんな僕にも潜む正義が どうしようもない衝動に駆られて ほら気付けば手を握っている
Isn't it time? The justice lurking even inside me blazes up, driven by a helpless impulse—look, before I know it, I'm holding your hand.

88
00:19:23,608 --> 00:19:28,608
いったいぜんたい そんなに荷物を背負い込んでどこへ行くの
Just what on earth are you going carrying so much baggage?

89
00:19:29,108 --> 00:19:36,608
ねえねえ待って僕にちょっと預けてみては?
Hey, wait, why don't you try entrusting a bit of it to me?

90
00:19:49,608 --> 00:20:04,108
信じてばかりの僕と 信じることが怖い君と
Me, who always believes, and you, who are afraid to believe...

91
00:20:04,451 --> 00:20:06,791
どちらが正しいのかなんて誰にも分からないさ
Nobody knows which way is right...

92
00:20:10,971 --> 00:20:14,711
僕らだけの世界
Our very own world...

93
00:20:20,161 --> 00:20:24,891
補い合えた暁には同じ夢を見たい
When we've supported each other, I want to dream the same dream.

94
00:20:40,541 --> 00:20:44,981
君はかっこいいと苦しめてひとりぼっちにさせ
Torturing yourself by thinking you have to be cool, leaving yourself all alone...

95
00:20:46,631 --> 00:20:52,561
たのは少し僕のせいなんだよな ごめんね
...is partly my fault, you know. I'm sorry.

96
00:20:54,191 --> 00:20:57,461
だけど見るべきはリアルだ
But what we need to look at is reality!

97
00:20:57,821 --> 00:21:06,521
今こそ僕が救けるんだ 抱えないで信じて頼ってほしいんだ
Now is the time I'm going to save you! Don't carry it all alone; believe in me and rely on me.

98
00:21:11,821 --> 00:21:16,311
今なんじゃない？ メラメラとたぎる こんな僕にも眠る正義が
Isn't it time? The burning passion sleeping deep inside someone like me...

99
00:21:16,571 --> 00:21:21,561
どうしようもない衝動に駆られて ほら気付けば手を握っている
...driven by an irresistible impulse, look, before you know it, our hands are clasped.

100
00:21:21,891 --> 00:21:25,451
ほっておけない
I can't just leave you be!

101
00:21:27,881 --> 00:21:38,351
そんなに荷物を背負い込んでどこへ行くの ほんのちょっと僕にちょっと預けてみては？
Where are you going carrying all that baggage? Won't you entrust just a little bit of it to me?

102
00:21:40,691 --> 00:21:45,351
こんな僕も君のヒーローになりたいのさ
Even someone like me wants to be your hero.

103
00:21:53,251 --> 00:22:04,451
ラララ...
La la la...

104
00:22:06,251 --> 00:22:15,451
ラララ...
La la la...

105
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:26,140
はい！みなさん！
Hi everyone!

106
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:35,190
とうとう始まってしまいました！天音かなた卒業ライブということでですね
It's finally started! This is Amane Kanata's graduation live...

107
00:22:36,540 --> 00:22:45,470
こちらハッシュタグが、あの #天音かなた卒業ライブ でございますので、ぜひこちらよろしくお願いいたします！
The hashtag for this graduation live is #天音かなた卒業ライブ, so please check it out!

108
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:55,610
1曲目に歌った荒野のヒースは実は初配信で歌おうか悩んでいた楽曲だったので、ここで歌えてすごくよかった！ありがと〜！
The first song I sang, "Kouya no Heath," was actually a song I debated singing in my very first stream, so I'm so glad I could sing it here! Thank you!

109
00:22:55,770 --> 00:23:03,160
え、小さい頃からね、ヒロインよりヒーローになりたいっていう僕のタイプだったので、そういった楽曲をたくさん歌わせていただきました！
Ever since I was little, I was the type who wanted to be a hero rather than a heroine, so I got to sing many songs like that!

110
00:23:03,730 --> 00:23:10,760
次からは、ありがとうねみんな、拍手もありがと！次からはロックで感情をぶつけていくような曲に
From here on—thank you everyone, thanks for the applause! From here on, we're moving into rock songs where I pour out my emotions...

111
00:23:11,070 --> 00:23:18,780
挑戦しますんで、ちょっとマイクが、調整しますんで、聞いてください！劣等上等！
I'll be taking on the challenge! Let me adjust my mic a bit... Please listen! "Rettou Joutou"!

112
00:23:38,129 --> 00:23:40,629
[Title: 劣等上等]

113
00:23:44,979 --> 00:23:46,579
劣等上等 BRING IT ON
Inferiority Superiority, Bring It On!

114
00:23:48,329 --> 00:23:50,029
列島上々 不眠日本
Archipelago upbeat, sleepless Japan!

115
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:53,629
子供騙しのマセマティカ バレてんだってそんなのって プライドがないや
Childish mathematics, they've figured it out, we have no pride.

116
00:23:55,629 --> 00:23:58,929
ご立派 警鐘 気取りで
Putting on airs as warning bells,

117
00:23:59,129 --> 00:24:01,929
高みの見物ばかりじゃつまんねぇ
Just watching from high above is no fun.

118
00:24:02,329 --> 00:24:05,429
ほらもっと 間違って上等
Come on, make even more mistakes, bring it on!

119
00:24:08,329 --> 00:24:09,929
ママ、やっぱあたしは
Mom, honestly, I...

120
00:24:10,129 --> 00:24:13,329
こんなところじゃ終われない
...can't end in a place like this!

121
00:24:14,129 --> 00:24:18,929
ぬるくて気が触れそう
It's so lukewarm I'm losing my mind.

122
00:24:19,329 --> 00:24:21,629
ごっこ遊びも芝居もさよなら ずっとこのままなんてさぁ
Goodbye to playing pretend and acting, staying like this forever

123
00:24:22,129 --> 00:24:26,629
いられないよ ダッダッダ あたし大人になる
I won't stay like that! Dad-dad-dad, I'm becoming an adult.

124
00:24:30,629 --> 00:24:36,129
パッパッパ 変わる時代 悪いことばかりじゃないでしょう
Pa-pa-pa, changing times—it's not all bad, right?

125
00:24:36,629 --> 00:24:40,629
過去も、罪も、罰も、すべて
Past, sins, punishments—all of them,

126
00:24:40,929 --> 00:24:44,629
素手で、愛で、生き抜いてやり返すわ
With bare hands and love, surviving and fighting back!

127
00:24:48,329 --> 00:24:51,929
挑発 あたし達はno doubt
Challenging you, we have no doubt,

128
00:24:52,129 --> 00:24:55,629
緑のアイツにばっか構ってんね
Always fussing over that green guy,

129
00:24:55,929 --> 00:24:59,929
さぁburn up いつになったら貰える合格 赤ペンいれてよ どこがダメなんですか
Come on, burn up! When will I get a passing grade? Put your red pen to work—what's wrong with me?

130
00:25:00,329 --> 00:25:02,129
酒女金... やっちゃってコンプラ
Drinks, women, money—doing whatever, compliance!

131
00:25:03,728 --> 00:25:05,808
冗談じゃん ブラックジョーク
Just joking, black joke!

132
00:25:06,628 --> 00:25:10,068
中指立てたくなるような事情 ありすぎて指が足りねえから
There are so many reasons to stick up our middle fingers, we don't have enough fingers!

133
00:25:10,308 --> 00:25:11,928
and what's up 最低？
And what's up, feeling low?

134
00:25:11,928 --> 00:25:13,388
もともとだろ bring it on
It's been that way from the start, bring it on!

135
00:25:13,388 --> 00:25:17,388
「まあまあ」なんか要らない 欲しがります死ぬまでは
I don't need any 'there, theres', I'll keep wanting until I die!

136
00:25:18,328 --> 00:25:21,368
伸びた背丈 育った街に投げキス 見せ場はこっから 覚悟しとけよ
Blowing a kiss to our tall stature and the town we grew up in, the highlight starts here, so get ready!

137
00:25:25,128 --> 00:25:29,948
ダッダッダ 僕ら大人になる カウンター狙い 最低な日々に
Dadada, we become adults, aiming for a counterattack in these lowest days

138
00:25:30,508 --> 00:25:35,828
眈々とかます一撃 誰も読めない先 まだあいこでしょ
Striking a calm blow, the unreadable future is still a tie, right?

139
00:25:36,688 --> 00:25:42,548
バグも、ロスも、ズレも、すべて 素手で、生きて！生き抜いて覆すよ
Bugs, losses, discrepancies—all of them, with bare hands, live! Survive and overturn them!

140
00:25:42,548 --> 00:25:44,748
劣等上等
Bring it on, inferiority!

141
00:25:57,528 --> 00:26:02,488
ダッダッダ くだらないことばっかが譲れない
Dadada, we won't compromise on silly things

142
00:26:03,308 --> 00:26:08,508
わかるか？あたしの美学 この馬鹿正直な拳ひとつが切り札
Do you understand my aesthetic? This brutally honest fist alone is my trump card

143
00:26:10,348 --> 00:26:15,708
がなる劣等 一抜けよさらば！
Roaring inferiority, graduating first, farewell!

144
00:26:16,468 --> 00:26:20,228
一番抜けを 狙ってさあ
Aiming to be number one, come on!

145
00:26:20,588 --> 00:26:22,848
劣等上等
Bring it on, inferiority!

146
00:26:41,108 --> 00:26:44,228
こんなもんじゃない
This isn't all there is!

147
00:26:44,228 --> 00:26:49,868
ダッダッダ あたし大人になる 酸いも甘いも噛み分けて今
Dadada, I'm becoming an adult, tasting both the sweet and sour now

148
00:26:50,088 --> 00:26:53,968
燦々 交わるミライ もう子供じゃないのわかるでしょ
Brilliantly intersecting futures—you know I'm not a child anymore, right?

149
00:26:54,768 --> 00:27:01,228
時代 機会 待ってくれない 素手で、捨て身で、生き抜いて上等だわ
Times and opportunities won't wait. Surviving with bare hands and desperation is top-tier!

150
00:27:01,668 --> 00:27:06,228
愛ある時代 それでは皆様お先に Bye, Guys!
An era filled with love. And now everyone, bye guys!

151
00:27:12,788 --> 00:27:18,748
それでは皆様 お先にバイバイ
And so everyone, bye-bye to you all first!

152
00:27:18,748 --> 00:27:21,408
フロアが盛り上がりました
The floor is getting super hyped!

153
00:27:47,606 --> 00:27:49,906
[Title: ぼくらの16bit戦争]
[Title: Our 16bit War]

154
00:27:49,906 --> 00:27:51,406
[Text: 作詞・作曲:sasakure.UK]
[Text: Lyrics & Music: sasakure.UK]

155
00:27:59,688 --> 00:28:03,488
どうしてこんな事になったんだ？ 誰も教えちゃくれないんだ。
How did things end up like this? No one will ever teach me.

156
00:28:03,588 --> 00:28:06,548
何がセイギだ 何がギセイだ "秩序"は僕を裏切った
What is justice? What is sacrifice? "Order" has betrayed me.

157
00:28:13,368 --> 00:28:17,088
はじめは微さな孔だったんだ 居心地だけは良かったのにな。
At first it was just a tiny hole, even though it was cozy.

158
00:28:17,448 --> 00:28:20,748
プロパガンダと呑めや詠えや、 孔はしだいに誇大化した
With propaganda, drinks, and chanting, the hole gradually grew exaggerated.

159
00:28:27,728 --> 00:28:34,808
相対 と 絶対 の 飽和水蒸機圧 都合 が善過ぎた大人達の 都合 に ひとつ また ひとつ と 未来 は 過去 を無視した
The saturated vapor pressure of relativity and absolutes—to suit the over-convenient adults, one by one the future ignored the past.

160
00:28:52,608 --> 00:29:02,788
65535 の テトラと ゼロ次元 の 理想 抱えていてもなお ひとつ またひとつとエデンは姿を消した
Even holding 65,535 tetras and a zero-dimensional ideal, one by one Eden made its appearance vanish.

161
00:29:09,268 --> 00:29:15,588
ぼくらの16bit戦争。 イデアの波に蝕まれるな 残された空間で僕は
Our 16bit war. Do not be eroded by the waves of Idea, in the remaining space I

162
00:29:16,148 --> 00:29:23,928
うかつに肘さえつけやしない ぼくらの16bit戦争。 アルトとエゴが交差する
cannot even carelessly rest my elbows. Our 16bit war. Alto and ego intersect.

163
00:29:33,248 --> 00:29:39,548
XYしか愛せない僕は Z（なに）を信じて生きれば善い？
Unable to love anything but XY, what should I believe in to live?

164
00:30:06,949 --> 00:30:16,089
ハガネに撃ち込めよと鴻鵠の警笛 肩越しに響く矩形波なる断末魔 アルカディアの鐘が鳴る日は来るのだろうか？
Shoot it into the steel, the swan's warning horn, a square wave echoing over the shoulder, a death agony—will the day ever come when the bell of Arcadia rings?

165
00:30:23,569 --> 00:30:38,809
ぼくらの16bit戦争 イデアの波に蝕まれるな 残された空間で僕は 今日もぐっすり眠れやしない
Our 16-bit war. Do not be consumed by the waves of the Idea, in the space left behind, I still can't sleep soundly today either.

166
00:30:40,369 --> 00:30:54,769
ぼくらの16bit戦争 アルトとエゴが交差する リットダウン ビットレートの積で 僕は"秩序"を裏切らない
Our 16-bit war. Alto and ego intersect, multiplied by lit-down bitrate, I will not betray "order".

167
00:30:55,369 --> 00:31:10,469
ぼくらの16bit戦争 世界を敵に回しても 表現し得ないものが絆される 現実（こと）が何より許せなかった
Our 16-bit war. Even if making the world our enemy, that unexpressible things are bound together—that reality was what I could never forgive above all.

168
00:31:10,709 --> 00:31:14,929
ぼくらの16bit戦争
Our 16-bit war...

169
00:31:37,009 --> 00:31:39,989
はーい、皆さんありがとうございます。
Hi, thank you everyone.

170
00:31:41,009 --> 00:31:45,529
ここにね、何があると思います？
What do you think is right here?

171
00:31:45,529 --> 00:31:46,589
水。
Water.

172
00:31:49,369 --> 00:32:05,149
今回は、あのー、けっこう歌に集中するラインナップで来てましたけども、トレンド1位っての本当ですかこれ？嘘かもしれませんけれど、本当かな？
This time, um, we came with a lineup focused quite a bit on singing, but is it true that we're #1 on trending? It might be a lie, but is it real?

173
00:32:05,309 --> 00:32:06,689
ガチかも。
Might be for real.

174
00:32:07,469 --> 00:32:09,429
ありがとうみんな！
Thank you everyone!

175
00:32:09,669 --> 00:32:21,009
ありがとう！かっこいいと言ってくれてるのを見ながら、メガホンマイクが手からすっぽ抜けかけましたよ。本当に焦ったわ。
Thank you! While seeing you say I look cool, my megaphone mic almost slipped right out of my hand. I was really panicked.

176
00:32:21,469 --> 00:32:37,889
ということでね、えーと、何かに挑んでいく曲みたいなのは好きなのでもともと、えー劣等上等と僕らの16bit戦争をお届けさせていただきました！ね、すごい大好きなかっこいい楽曲たちなのでぜひぜひ原曲もチェックしてみてください！
So, um, I originally like songs that challenge things, so I delivered 'Rettou Joutou' and 'Bokura no 16bit Sensou'! They're amazing, cool tracks that I love so much, so please definitely check out the original versions too!

177
00:32:38,809 --> 00:32:45,029
ちょっと待て、私VTuberなんだけど着替えは何秒かかると思う？1秒だ！
Wait a second, I'm a VTuber, so how many seconds do you think a costume change takes? 1 second!

178
00:32:47,409 --> 00:32:55,889
ほれ。すごいだろ？これがVTuber、バーチャルアイドルね！ではこのまま続けていくぞ！
Behold. Amazing, right? This is a VTuber, a virtual idol! Well then, let's keep going right like this!

179
00:33:34,269 --> 00:33:43,929
ロンリーガールはいつまでも 届かない夢見て
A lonely girl, forever dreaming a dream that never reaches...

180
00:33:44,729 --> 00:33:53,889
騒ぐ頭の中を掻き回して、掻き回して
churning and churning through the clamor in her head...

181
00:34:03,769 --> 00:34:13,349
「問題ない。」と呟いて 言葉は失われた？ もう失敗、もう失敗
Muttering "I'm fine," have words been lost? Another failure, another failure.

182
00:34:16,089 --> 00:34:23,009
もう一回、もう一回 「私は今日も転がります」と
Once more, once more— "I'll roll again today," she says,

183
00:34:28,329 --> 00:34:31,489
少女は行く 少女は行く
the girl goes, the girl goes.

184
00:34:31,489 --> 00:34:42,649
言葉に意味を奏でながら 「もういいかい？」 「まだだよ」 「まだまだ先は見えないの？」 息を止めるの、今
weaving meaning into words— "Are you ready yet?" "Not yet." "Can you still not see ahead?" Holding her breath, right now.

185
00:34:53,089 --> 00:35:02,369
ローリンガールのなれの果て 届かない向こうへ
The end of the rolling girl, to the other side that can't be reached...

186
00:35:03,036 --> 00:35:07,506
重なる声と声を 混ぜ合わせて 混ぜ合わせて
Overlapping voices, mixing them together, mixing them together...

187
00:35:07,856 --> 00:35:12,546
もう一回 もう一回 混ぜ合わせて 混ぜ合わせて
...mixing them together, mixing them together.

188
00:35:12,936 --> 00:35:22,486
「問題ない。」と呟いた言葉は失われた どうなったって良いんだってさ
'No problem,' I murmured, and the words were lost? Whatever happens is fine,

189
00:35:22,486 --> 00:35:32,066
間違いだって起こしちゃおうと誘う 坂道
inviting us down a slope to make even mistakes.

190
00:35:32,066 --> 00:35:42,146
もう一回、もう一回 私をどうか転がしてと 少女は言う 少女は言う 無口に意味を重ねながら！
Once more, once more, 'Please roll me over,' the girl says, the girl says, layering meaning into her silence!

191
00:35:42,836 --> 00:35:50,406
「もう良いかい？」 「もう少し、もうすぐ何か見えるだろうと。息を止めるの、今。」
'Are you ready yet?' 'Just a little more, thinking I'll see something soon. Hold your breath, now.'

192
00:35:50,816 --> 00:36:01,286
もう一回、もう一回 「私は今日も転がります。」と 少女は言う 少女は言う 言葉に笑みを奏でながら！
Once more, once more, 'I'll roll again today,' the girl says, the girl says, playing smiles into her words!

193
00:36:01,286 --> 00:36:11,546
「もう良いかい？もう良いよ。そろそろ君も疲れたろう、ね。」 息を止めるの、今
'Are you ready yet? That's enough. You must be tired by now, right?' Hold your breath, now.

194
00:36:11,546 --> 00:36:15,018
[Sign: ローリングガール]
[Sign: Rolling Girl]

195
00:36:22,818 --> 00:36:28,818
[Title: 誰も見てない夢を見ろ]
[Title: Dream a Dream No One Else Sees]

196
00:36:22,868 --> 00:36:28,968
今度こそ 生き返れない そう思った
This time, I thought I wouldn't be able to come back to life.

197
00:36:29,218 --> 00:36:33,418
ベッドの中 気付けばカーテンの隙間から
In my bed, before I knew it, through the gap in the curtains

198
00:36:33,418 --> 00:36:40,018
朝が生を教えた ああ 生きてたと安堵
morning taught me life... Ah, feeling relieved that I was alive,

199
00:36:40,018 --> 00:36:46,018
ああ 生きてしまったと絶望 まだやれるのか まだやらなきゃなのか
Ah, despairing that I had survived. Can I still do this? Do I still have to?

200
00:36:46,018 --> 00:36:50,518
いっそ無理矢理もがれてしまえば なんてね
should I just have everything torn away forcefully? Or so I thought.

201
00:36:59,018 --> 00:37:04,018
「僕は元気です」そう言って今日も笑って
'I'm doing fine,' I say, smiling today as well,

202
00:37:04,018 --> 00:37:11,018
心はがらんどうです 大げさな音がする ああ
my heart is hollow, making an exaggerated sound. Ah,

203
00:37:12,018 --> 00:37:19,018
終末の鐘の音か
are those the tolling bells of the end?

204
00:37:20,518 --> 00:37:27,018
それでもこの声が それでもこの口が
Even so, this voice of mine, even so, this mouth of mine,

205
00:37:27,018 --> 00:37:33,518
それでもこの喉が 千切れるぐらい叫ぶよ
even so, this throat of mine will scream until it tears apart!

206
00:37:33,518 --> 00:37:47,518
この腕が 真っ白なこの羽が 僕のこの命が「生きたい」と歌ってる
these arms, these pure white feathers, this life of mine sings 'I want to live.'

207
00:37:48,018 --> 00:37:54,518
できるなら愛されたい 許されたい ここにいたい 愛したい
If possible, I want to be loved, forgiven, to be here, to love.

208
00:37:54,518 --> 00:38:05,018
誰も見てない夢を見るよ だから 僕を見てろよ
I'll dream a dream no one else sees, so look at me!

209
00:38:08,018 --> 00:38:18,518
感情の捨て方はさ 粗大ゴミのシールを貼る 本音はいつも強がりの裏
How to discard emotions... you slap a bulky waste sticker on them. True feelings are always behind bravado,

210
00:38:19,018 --> 00:38:27,018
潰れる音がするんだ ああ 気付かれなかった
making a crushing sound. Ah, nobody noticed.

211
00:38:27,018 --> 00:38:36,518
ああ 気付いてほしいんだ それでも君が笑ってくれるなら いっそ心をなくしてしまえば
Ah, I want you to notice. Even so, if you can smile for me, I might as well lose my heart entirely

212
00:38:37,018 --> 00:38:51,018
「敵わない」なんて 一瞬でも思ったら負けだ 「叶わない」なんて 一瞬でもよぎったらやめだ
Thinking for even a second 'I can't match it' is losing. Thinking for even a second 'It won't come true' is quitting.

213
00:38:51,018 --> 00:39:04,018
何万の諦める理由があったとしても たった一つの勇気がこの手の中に
Even if there were tens of thousands of reasons to give up, a single courage is right within this hand.

214
00:39:20,518 --> 00:39:33,018
それでもこの声が それでもこの口が それでもこの喉が 千切れるぐらい叫ぶよ
Even so, this voice of mine, even so, this mouth of mine, even so, this throat of mine will scream until it tears apart!

215
00:39:34,018 --> 00:39:47,018
この腕が 真っ白なこの羽が 僕のこの命が「生きたい」と歌ってる
these arms, these pure white feathers, this life of mine sings 'I want to live.'

216
00:39:47,518 --> 00:39:59,223
できるなら愛されたい 許されたい ここにいたい 愛したい 誰も見てない夢を見るよ だから 僕を見て...
If possible, I want to be loved, forgiven, to be here, to love. I'll dream a dream no one else sees, so please look at me...

217
00:40:00,446 --> 00:40:14,023
誰も見てない夢を見せるよ だから 僕を信じて
I'll show you a dream no one else has seen, so believe in me...

218
00:40:39,323 --> 00:40:51,723
はーい！ ふーっ…みなさん、今のわ最後のオリジナル楽曲です！誰も見てない夢を見ろ！と、いうかね、本日24時にリリース！
Hii! Whew... Everyone, that last song was my final original track! "Have a Dream No One Has Seen"! And, you know, it releases tonight at 24:00!

219
00:40:52,223 --> 00:41:43,723
わあー！こちらのジャケット、おしおママに頼りにして探してくださいね、と頼みを。いや、この曲、あまりにも卒業ソングすぎるって思ったでしょ？これ実は卒業決める前に作られていた曲で、卒業決める前に、MVは明日ね、あの、明日の20時、もうかなたそがいなくなっても予約投稿というものがある、ネットには。ということで、明日の20時に投稿されるんですが、内容も実は卒業を誰も知らずに作っているということで、なんかこんな偶然の一致でそれっぽくなってしまいました。それを踏まえてまたなんてやねんと思いながら聞いてください、ひぐちあいさんにね作詞作曲していただいて、あの悪魔の子ねいっぱい歌ったりしたんで、超嬉しかったです。ありがとうございます！
Wow! This jacket illustration—please rely on Mama Oshio to find it, I asked her. Well, you must think this song is way too much like a graduation song, right? Actually, this song was made before I decided to graduate, and before that decision, the MV is scheduled for tomorrow at 20:00—even if Kanataso is gone, scheduling posts exists on the internet. So it gets posted tomorrow at 20:00, but the content was actually made without anyone knowing about my graduation, so by such a coincidence it ended up feeling fitting. Keeping that in mind while thinking "What is this timing?!" please listen to it. Higuchi Ai wrote the lyrics and music for me, and since I sang "Child of Evil" a lot, I was super happy. Thank you so much!

220
00:41:44,223 --> 00:41:53,223
[Title: 天音かなた 卒業グッズ] 卒業グッズがもう出てます！なんと出てる！ということで、それでは一つずつ見ていきましょう！まずは、こちら！
[Title: Amane Kanata Graduation Goods] The graduation goods are already out! They're actually out! So, let's take a look at them one by one! First up, this!

221
00:41:54,223 --> 00:42:23,723
はい！アクリルパネルです！可愛いでしょう！じゃん！こちらね、おしおママに想いをお伝えした上で、描き下ろししていただいたイラストになっております！もう本当にね、みんなに対して最後は「まあ、笑顔かな」とか「青い薔薇」というものを、あの当初からちょっとモチーフ的に入れたりすることがあったので、あのこちらでまた入れていただきました。可愛いでしょう？笑顔にしてもらいました。じゃお次は、こちら！
Yes! It's an acrylic panel! Isn't it cute? Ta-da! This illustration was drawn specially for us after I shared my feelings with Mama Oshio! She incorporated motifs like "Well, let's keep smiling" and "blue roses" that we've had since the beginning, so she added them in here again. Isn't it cute? She gave me a smiling face. Now, next is this!

222
00:42:24,723 --> 00:42:47,723
